## Install locally

```bash
python3 -m pip install -e .
__COMMAND_NAME__ --help
```

If a Python 3.9 venv still bundles pip older than 21.3, use the local editable
fallback after installing the declared backend requirements:

```bash
python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python3 setup.py develop
```

The target project defaults to the relative path recorded in `lov-cli.json`.
Set `LOV_CLI_PROJECT_ROOT` or pass global `--project-root` when the project has
moved.

## Agent usage

```bash
__COMMAND_NAME__ --json doctor
__COMMAND_NAME__ --json capabilities
```

Put global `--json` before the subcommand. Success emits one JSON object with
`ok: true`; failure exits nonzero and emits a stable diagnostic envelope.

